### Correlation results

\(\hat{J}_{\rm part}\) correlations with \(\hat{J}_{\rm syst}\) and \(\hat{J}_{\rm spec}\)

In central heavy-ion collisions (\(b\lesssim 3\) fm), \(|\vec{J}_{\rm syst}|\) and \(|\vec{J}_{\rm part}|\) become smaller as \(b\to 0\) while \(|\vec{J}_{\rm spec}|\) remains large; many spectators still exist in these collisions (as seen for example in Fig. 72) which carry a large lever arm. Because of this, \(|\vec{J}_{\rm spec}|\) and \(|\vec{J}_{\rm part}|\) are non-zero even as \(b\to 0\) (see Fig. 65). As \(b\to 0\), \(\hat{J}_{\rm spec}\) becomes more random and so, therefore, does \(\hat{J}_{\rm part}\) due

