Recall that the first-order event-plane angle, \(\Psi_{1}\), is described by the azimuthal distribution of (typically) higher-rapidity particles (\(|y|>3\)). The then-newly-installed Event-Plane Detector (EPD) provided ideal coverage and granularity in order to provide measurements of \(\Psi_{1}\) with good resolution,

\[R_{\rm EP}^{(1)}\approx\sqrt{2\left\langle\cos(\Psi_{1}^{ref.1}-\Psi_{2}^{ref. 2})\right\rangle}, \tag{50}\]

